{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented the compact-worker leg in scan_locks via the existing _existence_report helper, keyed on the canonicalised tracker's .rebar/ (inherits fix 13f78e3165's canonical-store keying — scan_locks canonicalises before deriving rebar_dir, exactly as compact_trigger does). Module docstring census updated to five legs. Tests: free store reports the leg free with no spurious holder; live-holder lock is info (named, aged, pid live, no finding); dead-holder lock is a stale-lock finding. RED confirmed before the edit (3 failures on the four-leg census), GREEN after; lint/typecheck/complexity ratchet green. NOTE on adjacent scope: snapshot GC (a3da2f4cce) added <snapshot-store>/gc/worker.lock — same detached-worker shape, but it lives on a different root (the snapshot store, not the tracker's .rebar/), so it needs its own root-derivation/staleness design. Filed as unanimated-detectible-cow (2b09-d231-2152-42d6, discovered_from this ticket) rather than scope-creeping here."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787354674431736001,"uuid":"eb90571e-e6a5-4646-80c5-94f658d3f308"}